DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((sin(x))^2-3*(3-x)+1)^3");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((cos((sqrt(x)))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-7, -4, 2, 9} U (9, infinity) U ({-7, -4, 2, 9}) U {-7, -4, 2, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -4, 2, 9})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(9, infinity) U (9, infinity) U (({-7, -4, 2, 9} U (9, infinity))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -4, 2, 9})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(([5, infinity))) U {-10, 9} U [5, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, 9}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [5, infinity))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[5, infinity) U {-10, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-10, 9} U {-10, 9})) U [5, infinity) U [5, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`16+19-18+1/11`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>17.0909090909,width=>9}
---

[`11+18+15+3/2`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(45.5),width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B)) \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup A \cap (A \cup A) \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-7, -4, 2, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cup (A) \cup A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B \cup ((A \cup B)) \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, 10, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, -1, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -5, -8, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -1, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 10, 9>") x Compute("<-5, -8, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, -8, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -1, 4>") x Compute("<-2, 10, 9>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -1, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, 9, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 8, -4, -9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, 9, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, 9, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 9, 0>") x Compute("<3, -1, -5>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, 9, 0>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -1, -5>") . Compute("<8, -4, -9>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>4)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
